# Classic Pong Game

A modern, browser-based implementation of the classic Pong game with a cyberpunk neon aesthetic and optional power-up mode.

## Features

### Game Modes

- **Classic Mode**: Traditional Pong gameplay - simple, clean, and nostalgic
- **Power-Up Mode**: Dynamic gameplay with automatic power-ups that activate every 5 seconds without scoring

### Power-Ups (Power-Up Mode Only)

All power-ups affect both player and AI equally for fair gameplay:

1. **SPEED BOOST** (Yellow) - Both paddles move 50% faster
2. **BALL ACCELERATION** (Orange) - Ball speed increases by 50%
3. **PADDLES SHRINK** (Magenta) - Both paddles become 30% smaller
4. **TWO BALLS** (Cyan) - A second ball appears on the field

- Power-ups last 5 seconds
- No repeating power-ups - always get a different one each time
- Visual feedback with glowing paddles and on-screen timer
- Power-ups reset when anyone scores

### Visual Design

- Cyberpunk neon aesthetic with cyan and magenta color scheme
- Glowing effects on all game elements
- Retro Courier New font
- Smooth animations and transitions
- Dark gradient background

### Audio

- Web Audio API generated sound effects
- Distinct tones for paddle hits, wall bounces, scoring, and power-ups
- No external audio files required

### Controls

- **Arrow Up/Down**: Move player paddle
- **Spacebar**: Pause/unpause game
- **Escape**: Return to menu

### Difficulty Levels

- **Easy**: Slower AI with delayed reaction time
- **Medium**: Balanced AI speed and response
- **Hard**: Fast AI with quick reactions

## How to Play

1. Open `pong.html` in any modern web browser
2. Select game mode: Classic or Power-Up
3. Choose difficulty level: Easy, Medium, or Hard
4. First to 5 points wins!

### Power-Up Mode Strategy

- Power-ups automatically activate after 5 seconds without scoring
- They affect both players equally, so adapt your strategy quickly
- Use TWO BALLS chaos to your advantage
- Shrunk paddles and accelerated balls force mistakes - stay focused!

## Technical Details

- Single HTML file - no dependencies
- Pure JavaScript (no frameworks)
- HTML5 Canvas for rendering
- Web Audio API for sound
- Responsive design
- ~550 lines of code

## Browser Compatibility

Works in all modern browsers that support:
- HTML5 Canvas
- Web Audio API
- ES6+ JavaScript

Tested on:
- Chrome
- Firefox
- Safari
- Edge

## Game Mechanics

- Ball speed increases slightly with each paddle hit
- Ball spin based on paddle hit position
- AI difficulty affects speed and reaction time
- Paddles cannot move off-screen
- Ball resets to center after each score
- Power-ups designed to force scoring and prevent long rallies

